From 42839417b341a145b98b9414658ec7739fd06237 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 14:15:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add AI damage analysis + circled report for owner reference
 photos
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Each reference photo is now scanned by Gemini for existing dents, scratches,
cracks, and chips the moment it's uploaded (fire-and-forget, same pattern
as the weekly inspection analysis). Results are stored per-shot on
car_reference_photos (new damage/analyzed_at/analysis_error columns) and
surfaced as a Condition Report on the reference-photos screen: a red badge
on any shot with detected damage, a report list below the photo grid, and
tapping an item opens the existing DamageOverlayModal (now reusable across
both inspection-photos and car-reference-photos buckets) with a circle
drawn directly over the damaged area using Gemini's bounding-box output.

Also adds a manual "Analyze for Damage" button so photos uploaded before
this feature existed can be scanned without needing to be retaken.

New analyze-reference-photo edge function (deployed) does the per-photo
Gemini call — unlike analyze-inspection, no baseline comparison is needed
since a reference photo is the baseline itself.
